  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements:\n1. Find the Customer Service on the Booking website\n2. Browse the questions about cancellation\n3. Provide the answer to 'how do I know whether my booking has been cancelled'\n\n## Screenshot Analysis:\n\n**Screenshot 1:** Shows the Booking.com homepage, which is the starting point of the task.\n\n**Screenshot 2:** Shows the Help Center page (\"Welcome to the Help Center\") with Customer Service contact options (\"Send us a message\" and \"Call us\" - available 24 hours a day). The Frequently asked questions section is visible with the \"Cancellations\" category listed. This confirms the Customer Service section was successfully located.\n\n**Screenshot 3:** Shows the Cancellations FAQ page with multiple cancellation-related questions:\n- Can I cancel my booking?\n- If I need to cancel my booking, will I pay a fee?\n- Can I cancel or change my dates for a non-refundable booking?\n- **How do I know if my booking was canceled?** ← Target question\n- Where can I find my cancellation policy?\n\nThis confirms the cancellation questions were browsed.\n\n**Screenshots 4 & 5:** Show the answer page for \"How do I know if my booking was canceled?\" with the following text: *\"After you cancel a booking with us, you should get an email confirming the cancellation. Make sure to check your inbox and spam/junk mail folders. If you don't receive an email within 24 hours, contact the property to confirm they got your cancellation.\"*\n\n## Response Verification:\nThe Result Response states: \"You can tell your booking has been cancelled because, after you cancel a booking with Booking.com, you should get an email confirming the cancellation. Check your inbox and spam/junk mail folders. If you don't receive an email within 24 hours, contact the property to confirm they got your cancellation.\"\n\nThis matches the content displayed in the screenshots exactly.\n\n## Conclusion:\nAll three task components were completed:\n1. ✅ Customer Service (Help Center) was found\n2. ✅ Cancellation questions were browsed\n3. ✅ The answer to the specific question was accurately provided\n\n**Verdict: SUCCESS**",
